WEBVTT

00:27.360 --> 00:32.130
All I’ve ever thought about was how to kill this man.

00:44.170 --> 00:47.480
My parents and I were running away from something.

00:47.760 --> 00:50.570
Who were we running from, and why?

00:51.100 --> 00:53.900
My memories are hazy, scrambled.

00:54.480 --> 00:56.530
I can’t even remember my parents’ faces.

01:10.120 --> 01:15.010
When I came to, had it been a short time, or maybe a few hours?

01:16.090 --> 01:20.850
I was laying there, dying, under my parents’ dismembered bodies.

01:21.180 --> 01:23.810
I’d no idea what had happened,

01:25.020 --> 01:31.820
but I could at least work out that I would soon be dead.

01:33.200 --> 01:36.910
All of a sudden, he was there, looking at me.

01:39.750 --> 01:41.030
<i>That katana…</i>

01:42.020 --> 01:46.210
<i>This man, was he the one who did this to us?</i>

01:46.440 --> 01:47.710
Do you want to live?

01:48.960 --> 01:51.130
I’m asking you whether you want to die or not.

01:54.350 --> 01:55.950
This man…

01:58.360 --> 02:01.430
And that was when I made my choice.

02:06.480 --> 02:07.370
It’s yours.

02:08.250 --> 02:10.300
Learn how to survive on your own.

02:11.620 --> 02:13.980
I don’t like teaching, so you’ll have to learn by watching.

02:14.970 --> 02:16.900
That’s how I did it.

02:23.610 --> 02:26.250
Use an enemy’s mistakes against them.

02:26.250 --> 02:27.660
Not bad, though.

02:28.820 --> 02:29.870
Do you hate me?

02:30.750 --> 02:32.550
Do you want to kill me?

02:33.270 --> 02:35.070
That’s fine, too.

02:35.070 --> 02:38.050
At least this way you won’t lose your murderous intent and end up an empty shell.

02:39.290 --> 02:41.340
What? His expression just now…

02:41.860 --> 02:44.850
By the way, have you managed to remember your name?

02:46.480 --> 02:49.190
I couldn’t recall my own name.

02:49.190 --> 02:52.010
My memory had disappeared due to shock.

02:52.010 --> 02:55.360
I couldn’t even remember my own name or the faces of my parents.

02:57.400 --> 02:58.810
Naoto.

02:59.670 --> 03:01.360
I’ll call you that for now.

03:01.910 --> 03:05.870
Until you can remember your own name, anyway.

03:06.280 --> 03:09.010
Even my name has been given to me by this man.

03:10.070 --> 03:11.870
I feel like throwing up.

03:12.970 --> 03:14.520
Hey, hey, what do we have here?

03:14.520 --> 03:16.090
Naoto, eh?

03:16.920 --> 03:19.130
Doesn’t that bring back memories.

03:19.550 --> 03:20.430
Magato.

03:20.900 --> 03:22.530
Where have you been?

03:22.530 --> 03:23.720
Working.

03:28.390 --> 03:31.630
Yo, Ms. Newbie. The name’s Magato.

03:31.630 --> 03:34.230
How do you do, Naoto the Second?

03:39.830 --> 03:41.650
A few years later…

03:42.020 --> 03:42.990
Still too slow.

03:47.300 --> 03:52.120
A knife, when used to attack from the side, is just like a piece of deadwood

03:52.120 --> 03:54.610
if your cutting and striking speeds are too slow.

03:54.840 --> 03:56.570
All it takes is a strike from the side,

03:57.610 --> 03:59.210
and anything can be parried.

04:11.870 --> 04:13.890
Well, something like that.

04:13.890 --> 04:16.070
That’s enough for today.

04:17.550 --> 04:18.840
I’m going out.

04:27.990 --> 04:32.000
I wonder how many years it’s been since you came here.

04:32.520 --> 04:36.420
You’re full of killing intent from day to night.

04:36.420 --> 04:39.750
You’re something else, I have to say.
Do you really want to

04:39.750 --> 04:41.260
kill him that badly?

04:41.260 --> 04:42.690
What are you trying to say?

04:44.130 --> 04:46.760
Don’t get all serious now.

04:47.060 --> 04:49.020
I was praising you, you know.

04:50.680 --> 04:56.020
Through all these years, you’ve actually grown up to be quite a beauty.

04:56.020 --> 04:56.730
Don’t touch me!

04:58.830 --> 05:00.580
No need to get snappy.

05:01.050 --> 05:04.820
Oh, yeah, you were cut by his katana, weren’t you.

05:08.260 --> 05:11.300
I knew it! This wound is from him!

05:11.300 --> 05:13.100
Just as I thought.

05:13.100 --> 05:14.160
It’s his swordsmanship.

05:14.340 --> 05:15.720
Get your hands off me, Magato!

05:16.440 --> 05:18.420
What a cute face you’re making!

05:18.420 --> 05:21.390
It’s such a waste, Naoto.

05:21.390 --> 05:24.010
You should be more aware of your beauty.

05:24.490 --> 05:27.040
People say a woman’s body is no longer beautiful after it’s been damaged,

05:27.040 --> 05:28.890
but it seems that is a lie.

05:28.890 --> 05:33.500
In fact, seems that somethin’ like this is more beautiful to me.

05:33.500 --> 05:34.730
Let go! Magato!

05:36.840 --> 05:38.440
Just when I was getting to the good part…

05:38.830 --> 05:40.360
It’s better if you just stop there.

05:40.850 --> 05:43.190
Don’t go and take my life away now.

05:43.480 --> 05:45.950
Can’t you take a joke?

05:46.350 --> 05:48.030
How about the weapon that’s pointing at me?

05:48.400 --> 05:50.550
Is that also a joke?

05:51.160 --> 05:54.980
’Kay, ’kay. I surrender.

05:54.980 --> 05:55.790
Magato.

05:56.220 --> 05:59.790
Lately, you’ve been idling around without doing any work. Is that on purpose?

05:59.790 --> 06:02.470
I’m not slackin’ off or anything.

06:02.470 --> 06:05.800
Just waitin’ for the right card to fall in my hands.

06:08.850 --> 06:09.680
Take it.

06:10.980 --> 06:16.100
That expression he made; I thought it was something distorted by the cracks on the mirror.

06:23.700 --> 06:29.000
For some reason, his shoulders seemed very small then.

06:37.600 --> 06:38.960
The newspaper.

06:38.960 --> 06:41.360
Good job as always, Nao!

06:41.360 --> 06:42.050
Thanks.

06:48.800 --> 06:49.740
I just got back-

07:03.970 --> 07:06.100
Welcome home, Naoto.

07:07.790 --> 07:10.220
Rejoice. Today is a great day.

07:10.220 --> 07:14.200
The special day for Magato, who has become a splendid adult, sparkling with radiance.

07:14.200 --> 07:16.700
Let’s celebrate it, Naoto.

07:16.700 --> 07:19.530
I’ve finally surpassed him.

07:19.530 --> 07:22.710
I’ve endured it for so long, <i>too</i> long.

07:22.710 --> 07:26.060
You told me to learn everything through real combat experience, didn’t you?

07:26.060 --> 07:28.210
Well, like you said,

07:28.210 --> 07:35.210
I continued part-timing as a sweeper in hopes that I’d get stronger, to answer your expectations.

07:35.210 --> 07:40.730
And, finally, I’ve won against you.
Isn’t that wonderful?

07:41.150 --> 07:44.220
No hard feelings just ’cause the circumstances, eh, Naoto?

07:47.180 --> 07:48.480
The faster one wins.

07:52.540 --> 07:53.530
Magato.

07:54.530 --> 07:55.740
I’ll kill you.

07:58.180 --> 08:02.740
My body suddenly moved at that instant.
A hateful voice burned in my throat.

08:03.580 --> 08:06.470
My emotions right then were in total disarray.

08:07.080 --> 08:10.550
When I came to, I was swinging my knife around recklessly.

08:26.760 --> 08:29.320
He’s fast. So, this is Magato’s—

08:35.240 --> 08:36.740
One more move.

08:37.160 --> 08:37.660
She dodged it?!

08:50.310 --> 08:53.550
You’re even better than I expected, Naoto,

08:53.550 --> 08:57.430
but you’re showing your hesitation.

08:57.430 --> 08:59.390
Still too naive!

09:07.920 --> 09:10.460
Wow, so close, so close!

09:11.040 --> 09:12.780
I am quite surprised, though, Naoto.

09:13.090 --> 09:15.520
You’ve grown this much.

09:15.520 --> 09:19.250
If you were fighting against him,
you might have actually won.

09:21.160 --> 09:24.460
But hey, at least you’re free now.

09:24.460 --> 09:27.290
Living for vengeance is pretty gloomy, you know.

09:27.740 --> 09:31.630
Why don’t you take what you’ve learned and live the way you want?

09:31.630 --> 09:33.630
Come with me, Naoto.

09:33.630 --> 09:35.480
Let’s reconcile.

09:35.480 --> 09:36.140
No thanks.

09:37.240 --> 09:38.540
I…

09:40.170 --> 09:42.010
I hate people like you!

09:55.240 --> 09:56.480
You’re so close, Naoto,

09:56.480 --> 09:58.550
but you’re still one second too late, so its my victory.

10:03.030 --> 10:05.250
You! That’s…

10:06.130 --> 10:07.790
All it takes is a strike from the side,

10:10.170 --> 10:12.170
and anything can be parried.

10:19.760 --> 10:21.380
Ouch.

10:24.480 --> 10:26.120
This is not good.

10:27.610 --> 10:31.500
Awesome. Looks like there’s one more important person for this anniversary.

10:31.500 --> 10:36.280
Just when Magato had finally became a splendid adult, he was beaten. Or something like that.

10:36.760 --> 10:40.960
Maybe it’s better if I include your name, Naoto.

10:42.620 --> 10:45.380
As a reward, let me tell you one thing.

10:46.290 --> 10:50.790
It’s about the real culprit behind the murder of you and your parents.

10:52.430 --> 10:56.800
I’m certain now, after seeing the wound on your chest.

10:57.100 --> 11:00.280
There’s another katana, exactly like that one.

11:01.080 --> 11:03.800
There exists another Naoto.

11:03.800 --> 11:06.810
He’s down there, in the underworld.

11:08.270 --> 11:10.120
You hid it from me?

11:10.120 --> 11:13.270
You two knew about it, but you hid it from me?

11:13.270 --> 11:14.050
Why?

11:14.650 --> 11:19.070
I told you, didn’t I? A life of vengeance is a stupid and worthless life.

11:19.740 --> 11:25.900
I have no past. Right now, I’m just trying to live without any regrets by following my own desires.

11:25.900 --> 11:29.080
But you, you have chosen your own path.

11:29.410 --> 11:33.080
I don’t like to hold back my feelings either,

11:33.920 --> 11:39.950
but by doing that, he managed to give you a reason to live.

11:40.610 --> 11:43.470
Maybe that wasn’t a bad thing to do after all.

11:46.170 --> 11:48.850
The katana. It’s yours.

11:49.210 --> 11:51.850
Where are you going, Magato?

11:52.550 --> 11:55.980
I’d like to choose my own resting place.

11:55.980 --> 11:59.480
If I’m lucky, we’ll meet again, Naoto.

12:24.200 --> 12:25.390
Can I ask you something?

12:27.190 --> 12:35.020
Why did you keep taking in all my hatred all these years without saying anything?

12:35.840 --> 12:38.520
You gave me the name “Naoto,”

12:39.040 --> 12:42.530
yet you’ve never once called me by that name.

12:55.490 --> 12:56.510
Hey.

12:58.010 --> 13:00.550
Why did you give me that coat?

14:30.870 --> 14:35.600
Presented by
